WEBVTT

00:00:03.397 --> 00:00:06.397
Look at that. Would you look at that?

00:00:06.477 --> 00:00:09.797
Filthy. Absolutely filthy.

00:00:09.877 --> 00:00:13.277
And it's all thanks to you, kid.
You made it possible.

00:00:13.357 --> 00:00:15.317
Jacques, I said no cleaning.

00:00:15.397 --> 00:00:16.477
I am ashamed.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.997
Look. Scum angel.

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:20.637
(CRIES OF DISTRESS)

00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:26.717
Bubbles! I love the bubbles. (COUGHS)

00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:31.397
Flo? Has anybody seen Flo? Flo!

00:00:31.477 --> 00:00:33.557
9:00, and cue dentist.

00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:36.277
Barbara. Sorry I'm late.

00:00:36.357 --> 00:00:38.557
Okay. Here we go.

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:40.277
Little Davey Reynolds.

00:00:40.357 --> 00:00:44.637
-Walks to the counter, drops the keys...
-Bloat, that's disgusting.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.037
Tastes pretty good to me. (BURPS)

00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.917
Don't you realize
we are swimming in our own...

00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:53.517
-Shh! Here he comes.
-What the...

00:00:55.077 --> 00:00:56.877
Crikey. What a state.

00:01:00.877 --> 00:01:03.997
Barbara, what's my earliest
appointment tomorrow?

00:01:04.077 --> 00:01:05.957
-10:00, love.
-Leave it open.

00:01:06.037 --> 00:01:09.597
I've got to clean the fish tank
before Darla gets here.

00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:14.517
-You hear that, Sharkbait?
-Yay! He's going to clean the tank!

00:01:14.597 --> 00:01:16.477
Yeah, we're going to be clean!

00:01:16.557 --> 00:01:18.477
-Ready to see your dad?
-Uh-huh.

00:01:18.557 --> 00:01:19.717
Course you are.

00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:25.597
I wouldn't be surprised if he's out there
in the harbor waiting for you right now.

00:01:26.397 --> 00:01:27.757
Yeah.

00:02:28.717 --> 00:02:30.117
Aagghh!

00:02:35.117 --> 00:02:36.597
(DORY LAUGHS HAPPILY)

00:02:39.637 --> 00:02:41.357
DORY: Whoo!

00:02:43.477 --> 00:02:47.477
Here comes a big one!
Come on. You got to try this.

00:02:47.557 --> 00:02:51.157
-MARLIN: Will you just stop it?
-Why? What's wrong?

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:54.037
-We're in a whale. Don't you get it?
-A whale?

00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:58.077
A whale! 'Cause you had to ask for help.
And now we're stuck here.

00:02:58.157 --> 00:03:02.397
-A whale? You know, I speak whale.
-You're insane. You can't speak whale.

00:03:02.477 --> 00:03:05.317
I have to get out. I have to find my son.

00:03:06.317 --> 00:03:11.077
I have to tell him
how old sea turtles are!

00:03:13.557 --> 00:03:14.557
(DESPAIRING GROAN)

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:19.997
(DORY WHOOPS)

00:03:22.037 --> 00:03:23.077
Hey.

00:03:25.477 --> 00:03:26.997
You okay?

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:35.277
There, there.

00:03:35.357 --> 00:03:38.037
It's all right. It'll be okay.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.557
No. It won't.

00:03:40.677 --> 00:03:42.957
Sure it will. You'll see.

00:03:43.037 --> 00:03:47.637
No. I promised him I'd never
let anything happen to him.

00:03:49.197 --> 00:03:52.957
Huh. That's a funny thing to promise.

00:03:53.037 --> 00:03:54.037
What?

00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:56.637
You can't never let anything
happen to him.

00:03:56.717 --> 00:03:59.317
Then nothing would
ever happen to him.

00:04:01.877 --> 00:04:04.157
Not much fun for little Harpo.

00:04:14.557 --> 00:04:17.237
-What's going on?
-Don't know. I'll ask him.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:22.717
-(MOOS) What's...
-Dory.

00:04:22.797 --> 00:04:24.277
...going

00:04:24.357 --> 00:04:26.437
on?

00:04:26.597 --> 00:04:28.277
(WHALE ROARS)

00:04:32.197 --> 00:04:35.317
-I think he says we've stopped.
-Of course we've stopped.

00:04:35.437 --> 00:04:39.157
Stop trying to speak whale.
You're going to make things worse.

00:04:39.237 --> 00:04:40.197
What is that noise?

00:04:40.317 --> 00:04:41.637
(ROARING)

00:04:44.637 --> 00:04:46.557
Oh, no. Look what you did.

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:51.477
The water's going down.
It's going down!

00:04:55.517 --> 00:04:58.757
-Really? You sure about that?
-Look. Already it's half-empty.

00:04:59.237 --> 00:05:02.837
-Hmm. I'd say it's half-full.
-Stop that. It's half-empty!

00:05:03.437 --> 00:05:05.117
(ROARING)

00:05:06.117 --> 00:05:08.717
Okay, that one was a little tougher.

00:05:08.797 --> 00:05:11.717
He either said we should go
to the back of the throat

00:05:11.797 --> 00:05:13.957
or he wants a root beer float.

00:05:14.037 --> 00:05:17.717
Of course he wants us to go there.
That's eating us!

00:05:17.797 --> 00:05:20.557
How do I taste, Moby? Do I taste good?

00:05:20.637 --> 00:05:22.717
Tell him
I'm not interested in being lunch.

00:05:22.797 --> 00:05:25.157
-Okay. He's...
-Stop talking to him.

00:05:31.637 --> 00:05:34.677
-What is going on?
-I'll check. What...

00:05:34.757 --> 00:05:37.397
No. No more whale.
You can't speak whale.

00:05:37.477 --> 00:05:39.077
Yes, I can.

00:05:39.157 --> 00:05:40.157
No, you can't.

00:05:40.237 --> 00:05:43.717
You think you can do these things,
but you can't, Nemo.

00:05:45.037 --> 00:05:46.317
(ROARING AND WHISTLING)

00:05:48.517 --> 00:05:50.597
-Okay.
-Dory!

00:05:54.157 --> 00:05:57.437
He says it's time to let go.

00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:59.757
Everything's going to be all right.

00:05:59.837 --> 00:06:01.837
How do you know?

00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:04.277
How do you know something bad
isn't going to happen?

00:06:04.957 --> 00:06:06.197
I don't!

00:06:19.717 --> 00:06:21.517
Aaaggghhh!

00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:31.557
(CACKLES) We're alive!

00:06:33.237 --> 00:06:35.277
Look. Syd-ney.

00:06:35.357 --> 00:06:37.317
Sydney! Sydney.

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.917
Sydney again.

00:06:40.037 --> 00:06:42.277
You were right. We made it!

00:06:42.917 --> 00:06:45.037
We're going to find my son.

00:06:48.237 --> 00:06:52.157
Thank you, sir.

00:06:52.237 --> 00:06:54.277
Wow. I wish I could speak whale.

00:06:54.357 --> 00:06:56.517
Now we find the boat that took him.

00:06:56.597 --> 00:06:59.397
-Right.
-Come on. We can do this!

